            <title>1.5.12</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:18:22 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>44</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.12</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Tag-colored folders now show their color, like Finder.</b> A folder with a color tag renders its icon tinted in the tag's hue — glyphs (the download arrow, the music note) and shading preserved — everywhere folders appear: the file list, icon views, Gallery, the preview panel, sidebar Favorites, the folder tree, and Home tiles. Previously the color only appeared for folders customized via Finder's "edit folder" feature, because macOS bakes the tint into the system icon only for those; plain tagged folders stayed blue. Files keep the tag dots, matching Finder.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
